  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 59. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 新築 — 建物を新しく建てること。\n2. 深度 — 深さの度合い。\n3. 振動 — 物が細かく揺れ動くこと。\n4. 親睦 — 人と人が親しく仲よくなること。\n5. シンボル — あるものを代表して表す印や物。\n6. 進歩 — 物事がよりよい状態に進むこと。\n7. 新米 — その年に新しく収穫した米。\n8. 新芽 — 新しく生え出した芽。\n9. 深夜 — 夜がすっかり更けたころ。\n10. 親類 — 血縁や結婚などでつながる家や人。\n11. 進路 — これから進んでいく方向や道。\n12. 神話 — 神々の働きや世界の始まりなどを伝える物語。\n13. 自画像 — 自分の姿を自分で描いた絵。\n14. 字形 — 文字の形。\n15. 時刻 — 何時何分かという時間上のある一点。\n16. 自室 — 自分の部屋。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
